    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for message. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements the <ref refid="classMessage" kindref="compound">Message</ref> facade. The five severity helpers forward to a private MessageImpl that writes a coloured, single-line record through trantor::Logger. The two startup helpers use a second MessageImpl that prints directly to stdout. get_color holds the severity-to-colour map, and removeNewLine flattens embedded newlines.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: This is the implementation behind nearly every log line the server produces. Code throughout the project calls <ref refid="classMessage_1a8945553f3f7f0e2dfa55d424b41c4886" kindref="member">Message::InfoMessage</ref>/ErrorMessage/etc.; those calls end up here, get coloured and cleaned, and flow into the configured logger. Keeping the formatting in one place means all log output looks the same and startup banners are clearly distinguished from runtime records.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Function overloading: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::unordered_map: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_map">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_map</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::ranges algorithms (std::ranges::replace): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/replace">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/replace</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
